Concepts: diegetic (in-world) vs non-diegetic (score, narrator); sound perspective (level, EQ and reverb match the distance from camera); sound bridges (J-cut: the next scene's sound starts early; L-cut: the previous one carries over); leitmotif (a recurring sound idea tied to a character or product).
